# BuildKit reads this (named `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`) when building with
# `-f infra/lifeos-node/Dockerfile`, keeping the build context small and, more
# importantly, keeping the host's stale `node_modules` / Rust `target` out of
# the image so the in-image `npm ci` / `cargo build` are authoritative.
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
services/target
.git
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
lifeos-blobs
infra/nango/data
infra/gowa
frontend
worker
docs
external
